================================================================================
Educational Use & Authorization Notice
================================================================================

Every experiment under this `sec/` path is **security teaching material**. It
exists for one purpose only: **education and defensive research** — helping
learners understand how a class of vulnerability works and why modern
mitigations defend against it.

Scope of authorized use
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Use only on systems and processes you **own** or are **explicitly authorized**
  (in writing) to test.
- The targets in these labs are built to run **locally and unprivileged**,
  attacking your own process. They model a vulnerability class for study; they
  are not tools for attacking third-party systems.
- Deliberately weakened build settings (for example, disabling compiler
  mitigations) are used solely to make the teaching target observable. Any
  normally built binary is protected by the mitigations these labs explain.

Prohibited use
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Do **not** use any code, payload, or technique from these experiments against
systems you are not authorized to test, against production environments, against
other people's equipment, or in any way that violates applicable law. Applying
publicly documented teaching techniques to unauthorized targets is the sole
responsibility of the user.

Disclaimer
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This material is provided "as is" for learning only. The authors and copyright
holders accept no liability for any consequence of its use (see the MIT terms
above).
